# The production chains on the basic content set, with no install: bread from the farm's grain through the mill and the baker, meat from
# the pig farm and the butcher, and fish from the fisher, each reaching the castle. It needs no install and no SIEDLER_DIR. Run it with
# seed 4455544685788642 and size 1 (picked with `mise run seed-info -- --content-set basic --seed 4455544685788642`):
#   sh tools/play-run.sh basic-production --game-view --content-set basic --seed 4455544685788642 --size 1 --fps 10
# On that map the castle's click places it at 15,5 (flag 16,6). Its start stock holds 16 planks, 11 stones, 3 grain, 1 flour, 1 pig, 2 meat,
# 2 bread, and 2 fish; a lake lies east of 18,5. Sites at 18,5 (small), 18,9 and 20,12 (large) have their flags at 19,6, 19,10, and 21,13.
#
# Where the settlers come from. The castle holds 20 first settlers, 5 of them without a job (CastleRoster). Every road's carrier and every
# worker without a tool takes a settler without a job, and the sites take builders and a digger. The bread chain needs 6 settlers without a
# job for its three roads and its three workers. The settler supply adds a settler without a job to the castle each period from the castle's
# placement on (docs/rules/new-settlers.md); a supply settler is made a knight instead when one is owed and the castle holds a sword and a
# shield. This seed gives the settler rate 23, a period of (60 - 23) * 50 = 1850 clock units, a new settler about every 231 ticks. In the
# bread game the mill's, the baker's, and the farm's workers are supply settlers (indices 20, 25, and 26 in the list, past the first 20).
#
# The script plays three games on the one seed, each from the start stock, so its counts start from known values and a check of one chain
# does not see the goods of another. The meat game and the fish game are each started fresh by `seed` to another seed and back:
#   1. farm, mill, and baker in one game: the farm's grain goes to the mill, its flour to the baker, and bread to the castle. The start
#      stock's 3 grain and 1 flour make at most 4 bread, so bread 2 can reach 6 without the farm; bread 7 proves the farm's grain. The game
#      reaches it at about tick 16400, and the fast-forward stops at 60000 ticks, so a stall fails the run;
#   2. butcher, then pig farm (built in turn: both sites at once leave the butcher without a settler): the pig farm's pigs reach the butcher, and meat rises past the
#      3 the start stock could give;
#   3. fisher: his catch reaches the castle (fish 2 -> 5).
# The rules are the basic set's stand-ins (ADR 0018).
expect seed = 4455544685788642
expect size = 1
wait 0.3
click-tile 15 5
wait 0.3
expect bread = 2
expect flour = 1
expect grain = 3
button Mill
click-tile 18 5
button Mill
click-tile 15 5
button Baker
click-tile 18 9
button Baker
click-tile 15 5
button Farm
click-tile 20 12
button Farm
click-tile 15 5
wait 0.3
expect-count building = 4
button Road
click-tile 16 6
click-tile 17 6
click-tile 18 6
click-tile 19 6
button Road
click-tile 15 5
button Road
click-tile 19 6
click-tile 19 7
click-tile 19 8
click-tile 19 9
click-tile 19 10
button Road
click-tile 15 5
button Road
click-tile 19 10
click-tile 20 10
click-tile 21 11
click-tile 21 12
click-tile 21 13
button Road
click-tile 15 5
wait 0.3
fast-forward until bread >= 7 max 60000
expect bread >= 7
shot bread 19 9 5 3
dump bread
list bread

# The next game: another seed and back starts a fresh game on this seed, with its 20 first settlers and its start stock again.
seed 1234567812345678
wait 0.3
seed 4455544685788642
wait 0.3
expect planks = 0
click-tile 15 5
wait 0.3
expect meat = 2
expect pigs = 1
button Butcher
click-tile 18 9
button Butcher
click-tile 15 5
wait 0.3
button Road
click-tile 16 6
click-tile 17 6
click-tile 18 6
click-tile 19 6
click-tile 19 7
click-tile 19 8
click-tile 19 9
click-tile 19 10
button Road
click-tile 15 5
wait 0.3
fast-forward until ticks >= 8000 max 100000
shot butcher-built 19 9 4 3
button Pig farm
wait 0.3
click-tile 20 12
wait 0.3
button Pig farm
click-tile 15 5
wait 0.3
expect-count building = 3
button Road
wait 0.3
click-tile 19 10
wait 0.3
click-tile 20 10
click-tile 21 11
click-tile 21 12
click-tile 21 13
button Road
click-tile 15 5
wait 0.3
fast-forward until meat >= 4 max 300000
expect meat >= 4
shot meat 19 9 5 3
dump meat
list meat

# The next game: another seed and back starts a fresh game on this seed, with its 20 first settlers and its start stock again.
seed 1234567812345678
wait 0.3
seed 4455544685788642
wait 0.3
expect planks = 0
click-tile 15 5
wait 0.3
expect fish = 2
button Fisher
click-tile 18 5
button Fisher
click-tile 15 5
wait 0.3
button Road
click-tile 16 6
click-tile 17 6
click-tile 18 6
click-tile 19 6
button Road
click-tile 15 5
wait 0.3
fast-forward until fish >= 5 max 200000
expect fish >= 5
shot fish 19 6 4 3
dump fish
list fish
